m/users/XianWorld/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f420bcd439d9ef580b2396419aade2ee9d8884d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commits/f420bcd439d9ef580b2396419aade2ee9d8884d8","html_url":"https://github.com/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commit/f420bcd439d9ef580b2396419aade2ee9d8884d8"}]},{"sha":"321fbe9e7ed3df3a75efbd6baa7f3604ed437e68","node_id":"C_kwDOUJxystoAKDMyMWZiZTllN2VkM2RmM2E3NWVmYmQ2YmFhN2YzNjA0ZWQ0MzdlNjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Richard Huo","email":"huodianyan@126.com","date":"2026-09-16T10:52:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"Richard Huo","email":"huodianyan@126.com","date":"2026-09-16T10:52:36Z"},"message":"Wiki: write paths from the root, refs/ for reference clones (batch 3/3)\n\nMechanical pass over the live pages. Two rules, and the second is the part that\ntakes judgment: a path inside this repository loses the microduck-diy/ prefix,\nand a path into a reference clone gains refs/. A repository *name* gets neither -\n\"the official stack is Rust microduck/ plus MuJoCo microduck_rl/\" is prose, not a\npath, and prefixing it would leave a sentence pointing at nothing.\n\nLeft alone on purpose: the microduck-diy in every GitHub issue URL, raw/ (which\nis immutable ingest), _archive/ (a snapshot of what was believed at the time),\nand the existing log entries.\n\nlocal-workspace-layout.md is rewritten rather than patched: it is the layout\nsource of truth and its whole premise changed. SCHEMA gains the path convention,\nand sources: entries become wiki-root-relative with refs/, which also settles a\nlatent off-by-one - two of them were already resolving one level too high.\n\nzero3w-bench-plan pointed a sample image at the repository's old tmp/, which no\nlonger exists after the move into temp/.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"10d128339baa669f694525de8b29264f16041685","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/git/trees/10d128339baa669f694525de8b29264f16041685"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/git/commits/321fbe9e7ed3df3a75efbd6baa7f3604ed437e68","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commits/321fbe9e7ed3df3a75efbd6baa7f3604ed437e68","html_url":"https://github.com/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commit/321fbe9e7ed3df3a75efbd6baa7f3604ed437e68","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commits/321fbe9e7ed3df3a75efbd6baa7f3604ed437e68/comments","author":{"login":"XianWorld","id":8578566,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1Nzg1NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8578566?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld","html_url":"https://github.com/XianWorld","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"XianWorld","id":8578566,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1Nzg1NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8578566?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld","html_url":"https://github.com/XianWorld","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a9a71036d9ae6f6e66cf7e69b81e50e900e798db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commits/a9a71036d9ae6f6e66cf7e69b81e50e900e798db","html_url":"https://github.com/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commit/a9a71036d9ae6f6e66cf7e69b81e50e900e798db"}]},{"sha":"6148c91dd537f288982b2ed5ac336d766875ad1a","node_id":"C_kwDOUJxystoAKDYxNDhjOTFkZDUzN2YyODg5ODJiMmVkNWFjMzM2ZDc2Njg3NWFkMWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Richard Huo","email":"huodianyan@126.com","date":"2026-09-16T09:55:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"Richard Huo","email":"huodianyan@126.com","date":"2026-09-16T09:55:59Z"},"message":"Close #4: the reported symptom never existed, and split the remainder to #11\n\n#4 was opened for \"the main controller and HAT are not talking DXL DATA\".\nRead-only scanning on /dev/ttyS2 settled it the other way: the HAT TTL path\nwas reachable all along. Two method errors had hidden that - the servo was\nstill at its factory ID 1 @ 57 600 and had never been written to the bus\nvalues, and dxl_ping.py computed CRC over the wrong scope so the packets it\nsent were malformed, with a self-test whose fake servo reused the same error\nand therefore went green over a real fault.\n\nAlso corrects the previous commit's mechanism. shutdown=52 does not latch an\ninput-voltage fault; the factory default 53 includes bit0 and robotd's 52\nclears it, so over-voltage merely clears Torque Enable while the servo still\nanswers Ping/Read. The 6.0-6.5 V ruling stands, but \"the wrong voltage\nmanufactures a zero reply\" was wrong and would have misattributed the symptom.\n\nGovernance gains principle 8: self-checks and loopbacks prove the two ends\nagree with each other, not that they agree with the spec.\n\nThe remainder moves to #11: settling the extra 0x55 byte in this kit's status\nframe via U2D2 + Wizard, scope waveforms, writing the bus values, and\nmeasuring the current-limit staging.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"827b8e5f80fc854503ef200970c68a13e4217641","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/git/trees/827b8e5f80fc854503ef200970c68a13e4217641"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/git/commits/6148c91dd537f288982b2ed5ac336d766875ad1a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commits/6148c91dd537f288982b2ed5ac336d766875ad1a","html_url":"https://github.com/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commit/6148c91dd537f288982b2ed5ac336d766875ad1a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commits/6148c91dd537f288982b2ed5ac336d766875ad1a/comments","author":{"login":"XianWorld","id":8578566,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1Nzg1NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8578566?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld","html_url":"https://github.com/XianWorld","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"XianWorld","id":8578566,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1Nzg1NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8578566?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld","html_url":"https://github.com/XianWorld","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7dad6d571e8937de22b3974bba3734261a1b74e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commits/7dad6d571e8937de22b3974bba3734261a1b74e5","html_url":"https://github.com/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commit/7dad6d571e8937de22b3974bba3734261a1b74e5"}]},{"sha":"7dad6d571e8937de22b3974bba3734261a1b74e5","node_id":"C_kwDOUJxystoAKDdkYWQ2ZDU3MWU4OTM3ZGUyMmIzOTc0YmJhMzczNDI2MWExYjc0ZTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Richard Huo","email":"huodianyan@126.com","date":"2026-09-16T08:27:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"Richard Huo","email":"huodianyan@126.com","date":"2026-09-16T08:27:56Z"},"message":"scripts(dxl_ping): fix CRC scope, add stdlib serial + status framing; #4 retest\n\nBench retest on /dev/ttyS2 (Radxa Zero 3W + HAT, 6 V bench supply):\n1 Mbps is silent, 57 600 answers as ID 1. The servo is still at factory\ndefaults, so the old \"1 Mbps + same servo\" premise does not hold.\n\nTwo real bugs surfaced, both now fixed and covered by self-test:\n\n- CRC-16 must cover the 4-byte header (FF FF FD 00 ... last parameter). The\n  old code excluded it, so a real servo discarded every packet, while the\n  self-test's fake servo mirrored the same mistake and stayed green. The\n  first bench scan therefore reported a false \"no reply\" at both baud rates.\n  Pinned by the published vector ff ff fd 00 01 03 00 01 19 4e.\n- This kit's servo replies with a non-standard status frame: a constant 0x55\n  byte sits between LEN and ERROR and LEN counts it (DATA + 4, spec says + 3).\n  The byte is on the wire and covered by the servo's own CRC (14/14 frames),\n  so it is not a parser artefact. Parsing it as spec shifts every register by\n  one byte and yields plausible-but-wrong values (model=45056, 1792.0 V).\n  The parser now disambiguates using the length each instruction must return.\n\nAlso:\n- Add a stdlib termios serial backend. The Zero 3W has neither pyserial nor\n  pip, so requiring the package made the procedure unrunnable on the target.\n  Validated end to end over a PTY pair.\n- self-test: replay regression built from the real captured frames.\n\nMeasured baseline (scripts/dxl_ping.py info, /dev/ttyS2 @ 57 600):\nmodel 1200, firmware 53, id 1, baud index 1 (57 600), return delay 250,\nmax voltage 70 (7.0 V), min voltage 35 (3.5 V), pwm slope 140, shutdown 53,\nstatus return level 2, hardware error 0, input voltage 5.8 V, 26 C.\nEvery value matches the XL330 eManual factory default, and shutdown=53\nconfirms the corrected reading: factory 53 includes the Input Voltage bit\nand robotd's 52 clears it.","tree":{"sha":"c702a9204080bd2e4ccf9c15ae850be01fc57e4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/git/trees/c702a9204080bd2e4ccf9c15ae850be01fc57e4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/git/commits/7dad6d571e8937de22b3974bba3734261a1b74e5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commits/7dad6d571e8937de22b3974bba3734261a1b74e5","html_url":"https://github.com/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commit/7dad6d571e8937de22b3974bba3734261a1b74e5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commits/7dad6d571e8937de22b3974bba3734261a1b74e5/comments","author":{"login":"XianWorld","id":8578566,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1Nzg1NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8578566?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld","html_url":"https://github.com/XianWorld","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"XianWorld","id":8578566,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1Nzg1NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8578566?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld","html_url":"https://github.com/XianWorld","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"21e2bb8b3ca2c40ca712aba08aeee57d63507194","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commits/21e2bb8b3ca2c40ca712aba08aeee57d63507194","html_url":"https://github.com/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commit/21e2bb8b3ca2c40ca712aba08aeee57d63507194"}]},{"sha":"21e2bb8b3ca2c40ca712aba08aeee57d63507194","node_id":"C_kwDOUJxystoAKDIxZTJiYjhiM2NhMmM0MGNhNzEyYWJhMDhhZWVlNTdkNjM1MDcxOTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Richard Huo","email":"huodianyan@126.com","date":"2026-09-16T07:47:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"Richard Huo","email":"huodianyan@126.com","date":"2026-09-16T07:47:44Z"},"message":"hardware: #4 method audit (M1-M6); add scripts/dxl_ping.py + wiki/concepts/dxl-bench-method.md\n\n- M1 confirm 6.0-6.5 V bus, but correct the mechanism: Shutdown(63) bit0 is\n  Input Voltage Error; factory default 53 *includes* it while robotd writes 52,\n  which *clears* it. Overvoltage kills motion (torque off, LED blinking), not\n  comms - a shut-down servo still answers Ping/Read, so it cannot produce the\n  \"zero reply\" symptom by itself.\n- M2 confirm 1 A pure-HAT / 2-3 A with Zero stacked, plus set the limit before\n  power-up (CC foldback sags the rail instead of cleanly disconnecting).\n- M3 evidence insufficient: the #1 baseline (port/ID/baud/firmware/voltage) was\n  never recorded anywhere; mark it as such and add a collection step.\n- M4 confirm factory-default probe order (ID 1 @ 57 600 fallback) in the flow.\n- M5 add a read-only, versioned Protocol 2.0 scan/ping script.\n- M6 adopt upstream setup-board.sh report() as the consistency baseline, noting\n  console=display only takes effect after a reboot.\n- Split hat-dxl-bus-debug.md (>200 lines) into dxl-bench-method.md.","tree":{"sha":"2cc4f8184e57bb2e6ed90814d481c9209d010fb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/git/trees/2cc4f8184e57bb2e6ed90814d481c9209d010fb6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/git/commits/21e2bb8b3ca2c40ca712aba08aeee57d63507194","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commits/21e2bb8b3ca2c40ca712aba08aeee57d63507194","html_url":"https://github.com/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commit/21e2bb8b3ca2c40ca712aba08aeee57d63507194","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commits/21e2bb8b3ca2c40ca712aba08aeee57d63507194/comments","author":{"login":"XianWorld","id":8578566,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1Nzg1NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8578566?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld","html_url":"https://github.com/XianWorld","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"XianWorld","id":8578566,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1Nzg1NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8578566?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld","html_url":"https://github.com/XianWorld","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ba465d5b7a286d8fc01af00e12e564bf6d65bf05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commits/ba465d5b7a286d8fc01af00e12e564bf6d65bf05","html_url":"https://github.com/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commit/ba465d5b7a286d8fc01af00e12e564bf6d65bf05"}]},{"sha":"ba465d5b7a286d8fc01af00e12e564bf6d65bf05","node_id":"C_kwDOUJxystoAKGJhNDY1ZDViN2EyODZkOGZjMDFhZjAwZTEyZTU2NGJmNmQ2NWJmMDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Richard Huo","email":"huodianyan@126.com","date":"2026-09-16T06:58:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"Richard Huo","email":"huodianyan@126.com","date":"2026-09-16T06:58:03Z"},"message":"Ruling: DXL bus on the bench runs at 6.0-6.5 V, and the current limit is staged\n\nThe procedure and Issue #4 both prescribed 7.4 V, copied from the NP-F pack's\nnominal voltage. That conflicts with the project's own measurement: these\nXL330s are rated 3.7-6.0 V with a default Max Voltage Limit around 7.0 V, and\nthey alarm at ~7.2 V.\n\nThe reason this matters more than a spec-sheet disagreement is robotd's\nshutdown=52 mask, which latches an input-voltage fault and holds torque off.\nThe wrong rail voltage can therefore produce a servo that never answers -\nexactly the zero-reply symptom this Issue exists to chase. J13/J14 pin 2 is\n+BATT and the servos sit ahead of the buck, so the supply voltage is the\nservo's voltage with nothing in between.\n\nCurrent limit is split so a tripped limit cannot masquerade as a fault: 1 A\nfor the bare-HAT stage, 2-3 A once the Zero is on the rail, since its boot\npeak exceeds 1 A and a collapsed rail reads as a board that will not start.\n\nUpdated the Issue body plus hat-dxl-bus-debug, bench-power-supply,\nhat-solder-kit (7.4 V now scoped to bare-HAT only) and bam-identification-bench.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"a1d21006706df7377e6c1edbe0b541dcd9dd0681","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/git/trees/a1d21006706df7377e6c1edbe0b541dcd9dd0681"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/git/commits/ba465d5b7a286d8fc01af00e12e564bf6d65bf05","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commits/ba465d5b7a286d8fc01af00e12e564bf6d65bf05","html_url":"https://github.com/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commit/ba465d5b7a286d8fc01af00e12e564bf6d65bf05","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ScrapMeta/microduck-diy/commits/ba465d5b7a286d8fc01af00e12e564bf6d65bf05/comments","author":{"login":"XianWorld","id":8578566,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1Nzg1NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8578566?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld","html_url":"https://github.com/XianWorld","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XianWorld/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subs